One mole of an ideal monatomic gas is taken through a cycle of four steps:
(1) at constant volume V₀, the pressure rises from P₀ to 2P₀;
(2) at constant pressure 2P₀, the volume increases from V₀ to 2V₀;
(3) at constant volume 2V₀, the pressure falls from 2P₀ to P₀;
(4) at constant pressure P₀, the volume decreases from 2V₀ to V₀.
The efficiency of this cycle is:
